 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook 06 — Cluster Analysis & Product Recommender\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal**: Profile each cluster, give them business-meaningful names, and build a product recommendation engine.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What you'll learn:**\n",
    "- How to interpret and name clusters (the \"so what?\" of unsupervised ML)\n",
    "- Building a rule-based recommender on top of ML output\n",
    "- Using the full pipeline on new customers\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append('..')\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/customers_clustered.csv')\n",
    "print(f'Loaded {len(df)} clustered customers')\n",
    "print('Cluster distribution:')\n",
    "print(df['cluster'].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Profile each cluster\n",
    "\n",
    "We compute the mean of each feature per cluster.\n",
    "This tells us: \"what does a typical customer in each cluster look like?\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PROFILE_FEATURES = [\n",
    "    'age', 'annual_income', 'monthly_spending',\n",
    "    'savings_balance', 'credit_score', 'loan_amount',\n",
    "    'num_existing_products', 'months_as_customer'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster_profiles = df.groupby('cluster')[PROFILE_FEATURES].mean().round(0)\n",
    "print('Cluster Profiles (mean values):')\n",
    "print(cluster_profiles.T.to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize profiles as a radar/bar comparison\n",
    "# Normalize features to 0-1 range for fair comparison on same axis\n",
    "profiles_norm = (cluster_profiles - cluster_profiles.min()) / (cluster_profiles.max() - cluster_profiles.min())\n",
    "\n",
    "profiles_norm.T.plot(kind='bar', figsize=(14, 6), colormap='tab10')\n",
    "plt.title('Cluster Profiles (normalized 0-1 per feature)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Feature')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Relative Value (0=min, 1=max across clusters)')\n",
    "plt.legend(title='Cluster', bbox_to_anchor=(1.01, 1))\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=30, ha='right')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Name the clusters\n",
    "\n",
    "Look at the profile above and give each cluster a business-meaningful name.\n",
    "This is the most human step in ML — translating numbers into insight."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# We'll assign names based on the dominant characteristics\n",
    "# Run the profile table above to identify which cluster has what traits\n",
    "\n",
    "# Automated naming based on profile stats\n",
    "def name_cluster(row: pd.Series) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Assign a name to a cluster based on its mean feature values.\n",
    "    Uses simple heuristics on income, savings, credit score, and loan amount.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    income   = row['annual_income']\n",
    "    savings  = row['savings_balance']\n",
    "    credit   = row['credit_score']\n",
    "    loan     = row['loan_amount']\n",
    "    age      = row['age']\n",
    "\n",
    "    if income > 90_000 and savings > 60_000:\n",
    "        return 'High Earner'\n",
    "    elif income < 35_000 and loan > 20_000 and credit < 620:\n",
    "        return 'Debt Stressed'\n",
    "    elif savings > 20_000 and credit > 700 and age > 38:\n",
    "        return 'Stable Saver'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Young Spender'\n",
    "\n",
    "cluster_names = {c: name_cluster(cluster_profiles.loc[c]) for c in cluster_profiles.index}\n",
    "print('Cluster assignments:')\n",
    "for cluster_id, name in cluster_names.items():\n",
    "    dominant_archetype = df[df['cluster'] == cluster_id]['archetype'].value_counts().idxmax()\n",
    "    print(f'  Cluster {cluster_id} → \"{name}\"  (true dominant: {dominant_archetype})')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Add segment name to the DataFrame\n",
    "df['segment'] = df['cluster'].map(cluster_names)\n",
    "print('Segment distribution:')\n",
    "print(df['segment'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Product Recommendation Logic\n",
    "\n",
    "Now that we know which segment each customer belongs to, we can recommend the right product.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Segment | Recommended Product | Reasoning |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Young Spender | Premium Cashback Credit Card | High spending, wants rewards |\n",
    "| Stable Saver | High-Yield Savings Account | Already saving, wants growth |\n",
    "| High Earner | Investment Portfolio / Wealth Management | High income and savings, ready to invest |\n",
    "| Debt Stressed | Debt Consolidation Loan | Reduce interest burden |\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a **rule-based recommender** — the rules come from business knowledge, the clusters come from ML. Together they're powerful."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PRODUCT_MAP = {\n",
    "    'Young Spender': {\n",
    "        'product': 'Premium Cashback Credit Card',\n",
    "        'pitch': 'Earn up to 5% cashback on every transaction. No annual fee for the first year.',\n",
    "        'upsell': 'Starter Savings Plan — build your emergency fund while you spend smart.'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'Stable Saver': {\n",
    "        'product': 'High-Yield Savings Account',\n",
    "        'pitch': 'Earn 4.8% APY on your savings, with no minimum balance requirement.',\n",
    "        'upsell': 'Fixed Deposit — lock in a higher rate for 12-24 months.'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'High Earner': {\n",
    "        'product': 'Wealth Management Portfolio',\n",
    "        'pitch': 'Personalized investment strategy with a dedicated advisor. Minimum £50k.',\n",
    "        'upsell': 'Private Banking Suite — exclusive benefits, priority service, travel perks.'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'Debt Stressed': {\n",
    "        'product': 'Debt Consolidation Loan',\n",
    "        'pitch': 'Combine your debts into one low-rate monthly payment. Up to 60-month terms.',\n",
    "        'upsell': 'Free Financial Health Check with our advisors.'\n",
    "    },\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def recommend(segment: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    return PRODUCT_MAP.get(segment, {'product': 'General Banking Package', 'pitch': 'Contact us to discuss your options.', 'upsell': ''})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply to all customers\n",
    "df['recommended_product'] = df['segment'].apply(lambda s: recommend(s)['product'])\n",
    "df['pitch']               = df['segment'].apply(lambda s: recommend(s)['pitch'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Sample recommendations:')\n",
    "df[['customer_id', 'segment', 'recommended_product']].groupby('segment').head(2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Summary: how many customers get each recommendation\n",
    "print('Product recommendation distribution:')\n",
    "print(df['recommended_product'].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "df['recommended_product'].value_counts().plot(kind='bar', color='steelblue', edgecolor='white')\n",
    "plt.title('Customers per Recommended Product')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Product')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Customers')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=15, ha='right')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Full Pipeline: Recommend for a New Customer\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's tie everything together. Given a new customer's raw data, we:\n",
    "1. Preprocess (impute + scale)\n",
    "2. Apply PCA\n",
    "3. Predict cluster with KMeans\n",
    "4. Map to segment name\n",
    "5. Recommend a product"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load saved models\n",
    "preprocessing_pipeline = joblib.load('../data/preprocessing_pipeline.pkl')\n",
    "pca_model              = joblib.load('../data/pca_model.pkl')\n",
    "kmeans_model           = joblib.load('../data/kmeans_model.pkl')\n",
    "\n",
    "FEATURES = [\n",
    "    'age', 'annual_income', 'monthly_spending', 'savings_balance',\n",
    "    'credit_score', 'loan_amount', 'num_existing_products',\n",
    "    'months_as_customer', 'spending_ratio', 'savings_ratio'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict_segment_and_recommend(customer: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Given a raw customer dict, return segment name and product recommendation.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Step 1: build a 1-row DataFrame\n",
    "    row = pd.DataFrame([customer])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 2: add engineered features\n",
    "    row['spending_ratio'] = row['monthly_spending'] / (row['annual_income'] / 12)\n",
    "    row['savings_ratio']  = row['savings_balance'] / row['annual_income']\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 3: preprocess (impute + scale)\n",
    "    X_preprocessed = preprocessing_pipeline.transform(row[FEATURES])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 4: PCA\n",
    "    X_pca = pca_model.transform(X_preprocessed)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 5: cluster prediction\n",
    "    cluster_id = kmeans_model.predict(X_pca)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 6: name + recommend\n",
    "    segment = cluster_names[cluster_id]\n",
    "    rec     = recommend(segment)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        'cluster': cluster_id,\n",
    "        'segment': segment,\n",
    "        'recommended_product': rec['product'],\n",
    "        'pitch': rec['pitch'],\n",
    "        'upsell': rec['upsell'],\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test with example customers\n",
    "example_customers = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        'name': 'Alice (young, high spender)',\n",
    "        'age': 24, 'annual_income': 31000, 'monthly_spending': 2400,\n",
    "        'savings_balance': 1800, 'credit_score': 605, 'loan_amount': 7000,\n",
    "        'num_existing_products': 1, 'months_as_customer': 12\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        'name': 'Bob (mid-career, good saver)',\n",
    "        'age': 44, 'annual_income': 62000, 'monthly_spending': 2600,\n",
    "        'savings_balance': 38000, 'credit_score': 740, 'loan_amount': 4000,\n",
    "        'num_existing_products': 3, 'months_as_customer': 84\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        'name': 'Carol (high earner)',\n",
    "        'age': 51, 'annual_income': 145000, 'monthly_spending': 6000,\n",
    "        'savings_balance': 110000, 'credit_score': 800, 'loan_amount': 12000,\n",
    "        'num_existing_products': 5, 'months_as_customer': 120\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        'name': 'David (debt stressed)',\n",
    "        'age': 36, 'annual_income': 27000, 'monthly_spending': 2900,\n",
    "        'savings_balance': 900, 'credit_score': 540, 'loan_amount': 36000,\n",
    "        'num_existing_products': 1, 'months_as_customer': 36\n",
    "    },\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "for customer in example_customers:\n",
    "    name = customer.pop('name')\n",
    "    result = predict_segment_and_recommend(customer)\n",
    "    print(f'Customer: {name}')\n",
    "    print(f'  Segment:   {result[\"segment\"]}')\n",
    "    print(f'  Product:   {result[\"recommended_product\"]}')\n",
    "    print(f'  Pitch:     {result[\"pitch\"]}')\n",
    "    print(f'  Upsell:    {result[\"upsell\"]}')\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Final Summary — What you built\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Raw customer data\n",
    "       ↓\n",
    "  EDA (understand the data)\n",
